Project lineage
---------------

Glenn.jl is the Julia implementation of this library. Its Python counterpart,
pyglenn (https://github.com/ProfLeao/pyglenn), is maintained by the same author
and shares the same underlying dataset and the same NASA-7 evaluation
conventions. The two projects are kept feature-compatible where the language
allows, so results obtained with one can be reproduced with the other.

Glenn.jl is an independent implementation: no source code from pyglenn is
included in this repository.


Thermodynamic data
------------------

The file `data/thermo.inp` and the derived database `data/thermo.db` are built
from the thermodynamic database distributed with the NASA Glenn Computer
Program for Calculating of Complex Chemical Equilibrium Compositions and
Applications (CEA). That database is a work of the United States Government and
is in the public domain; it is redistributed here unmodified, except for the
parser fixes documented in `docs/PARSER_FIX_PORTING.md`.

Please cite the original NASA sources when publishing results that rely on the
bundled coefficients:

  * McBride, B. J., Zehe, M. J., and Gordon, S. (2002).
    NASA Glenn Coefficients for Calculating Thermodynamic Properties of
    Individual Species. NASA/TP-2002-211556.
    National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Glenn Research Center.

  * Gordon, S., and McBride, B. J. (1994).
    Computer Program for Calculation of Complex Chemical Equilibrium
    Compositions and Applications. I. Analysis. NASA RP-1311.
    National Aeronautics and Space Administration, Lewis Research Center.

The identifier "NASA Glenn" is used descriptively to refer to the origin of the
data. This project is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by NASA.


Validation reference data
-------------------------

The cross-validation script `docs/audit/audit.jl` compares computed properties
against the NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables, 4th edition:

  * Chase, M. W., Jr. (1998). NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables, 4th edition.
    Journal of Physical and Chemical Reference Data, Monograph No. 9.
    https://doi.org/10.18434/T42S31

Only the Shomate coefficients needed to recompute the reference values are
embedded in the script. No NIST data files are redistributed. NIST-JANAF data
are works of the United States Government and are in the public domain.


